  <!-- ── Narrative ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="narrative">
    <div class="narrative-inner">
      <div class="narrative-body">
        <p class="narrative-body-illuminated">
          <span class="drop-cap">I</span> have been writing code for forty years: first with
          assembly, then with high-level languages, then with AI. My 35 years in the tech industry
          includes almost two decades split between Amazon (1998-2005) and Google (2005-2017).
        </p>
        <p>
          I've also been writing <em>about</em> code, and the industry in general, since 2004.
          My writing has impacted companies, boardrooms, entire generations of programmers.
          My essays may not all be great, or even good, or even readable. But I've got some
          bangers in there.
        <p>
          Today, with <a href="gastown.html">Gas Town, Beads, and Gas City</a>,
          I am exploring what the future looks like with multi-agent and orchestration.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

